<article class="env-definition" id="04FS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04FS">Definition <span data-tag="04FS">59.31.3</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be an abelian sheaf on $S_{\acute{e}tale}$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
The <em>support of $\mathcal{F}$</em> is the set of points $s \in S$ such that $\mathcal{F}_{\overline{s}} \not= 0$ for any (some) geometric point $\overline{s}$ lying over $s$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Let $\sigma \in \mathcal{F}(U)$ be a section. The <em>support of $\sigma $</em> is the closed subset $U \setminus W$, where $W \subset U$ is the largest open subset of $U$ on which $\sigma $ restricts to zero (see Lemma <a href="/tag/04FR" data-tag="04FR">59.31.2</a>). 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>